Dusk Client 1.8.9 — ported behaviours and their sources
========================================================

Each entry names what was borrowed and under what terms. Code carried over
verbatim or adapted is marked "ported"; where only the behaviour was
reimplemented from reading a project (or its licence forbids copying), the
entry says "behaviour only" and no code from that project is included.

Build setup
-----------
- nea89o's Forge1.8.9Template (Unlicense): the Gradle/Loom build this project
  is assembled with.
- Jabel (Apache-2.0, bsideup; pkware fork): javac plugin used at build time
  so modern Java syntax compiles to Java 8 bytecode. Not shipped in the jar.

Framework (ids, settings, config shape)
---------------------------------------
- Dusk's own client-mod for 1.21.11 (GPL-3.0, this repository): module and
  setting framework, HUD renderer and every module's setting ids and saved
  form, ported so configs copy between versions.

Modules
-------
- ToggleSprint/ToggleSneak (Zlib, boogiemonster1o1's Mod Menu sibling
  ToggleSprint options mods): latched sprint/sneak behaviour, ported.
- Combo counter (MIT, Eymistaken's ComboCounter): combo tracking and reset
  rules, ported.
- Flex-HUD (crosshair presets, TNT countdown, TPS estimate): crosshair
  preset grids and the TPS rolling average, ported with thanks.
- PolyNametag (licence per repository): nametag scale/colour/background
  settings, behaviour only where the licence is not permissive.
- OverflowParticles: particle gating, recolouring and multiplier behaviour;
  behaviour only.
- DamageTint (part of Dusk's client-mod, GPL-3.0): hurt-tint replacement,
  ported.
- Custom Block Highlight (CBH): outline/fill/through-walls selection box,
  behaviour only.
- BactroMod (Low Fire): lowered first-person fire, behaviour only.
- Gamma Utils (Fullbright): uncapped gamma via the lightmap hook, behaviour
  only.
- natural-motionblur (and Dusk's own 1.21.11 renderer, GPL-3.0): motion blur
  accumulation/blend passes, ported from Dusk's renderer.
- Sodium (LGPL-3.0) and Input Optimizer: CPU render-ahead limiting via GL
  fences for Low Input Lag, behaviour only.
- Zoomify / Ok Zoomer: zoom easing, scroll adjustment and cinematic camera
  scaling, behaviour only.
- Mouse Tweaks (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2023 Ivan Molodetskikh / YaLTeR,
  https://github.com/YaLTeR/MouseTweaks): drag and scroll-wheel inventory
  logic, rewritten for 1.8.9's GuiContainer in modules/misc/MouseTweaks.java.

Cosmetics
---------
- Dusk's own client-mod for 1.21.11 (GPL-3.0, this repository): the cape
  registry, loadout format, Dusk service client and cosmetics manager,
  ported to Java 8 in cosmetics/.
- MinecraftCapes mod (LGPL-2.1,
  https://github.com/MinecraftCapes/minecraftcapes-mod): behaviour only.
  Replicated: the profile API contract (api.minecraftcapes.net), the
  offline-UUID resolution rule, the on-disk cache layout
  (<type>/<hash[0:2]>/<hash>), the animated-cape frame rule (height !=
  width/2 -> frames of width/2 rows, 100 ms each), the static cape padding
  rule and the 14x7 ears UVs. No source files were copied.
- The cape glint reuses vanilla 1.8.9's armour-glint passes (LayerArmorBase).

The 1.8.9 mappings for Minecraft itself come from MCP (mcp_stable 22-1.8.9),
used under its licence; Forge 1.8.9 is LGPL-2.1.

